#
# Abstract
# --------
# The runtime dependencies of PyTorch. The test, coverage, integration and
# model zoo workflows install PyTorch itself with --no-deps from
# requirements-ci-torch.txt, because the PyTorch index does not publish the
# hashes of most other files and serves outdated releases of some of them.
# `make lock` compiles these requirements from PyPI together with the extras
# of pyproject.toml into requirements-ci-test.txt, with a SHA-256 hash for
# every distribution. Keep the list in step with the requirements of the
# PyTorch release in requirements-ci-torch.txt.
# =============================================================================

filelock  # Locks for the PyTorch caches.
fsspec>=0.8.5  # File system abstraction used by PyTorch.
jinja2  # Templates of the PyTorch code generators.
networkx>=2.5.1  # Graphs of torch.fx and the compiler.
setuptools>=77.0.3  # Build helpers that PyTorch imports.
sympy>=1.13.3  # Symbolic shapes of the PyTorch compiler.
typing-extensions>=4.10.0  # Typing backports used by PyTorch.

